00:08:41.949 --> 00:08:47.869
So first of all, why do I think that the Gorosei
are actually very powerful and will be actual

00:08:47.869 --> 00:08:50.790
enemies that have to be taken down?

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:56.809
Because I've seen a lot of opinions stating
that the Gorosei are basically glorified Spandams.

00:08:56.809 --> 00:09:01.589
That's this guy in case you forgot.

00:09:01.589 --> 00:09:06.509
[] The reason Spandam was able to control
some of the governments most powerful agents

00:09:06.509 --> 00:09:12.139
was not because he was smart enough to manipulate
them, but because they were ordered by the

00:09:12.139 --> 00:09:15.160
government, in other words the gorosei to
help him.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.191
Now you could say that the main source of
authority for the Gorosei is that they have

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:22.819
both the Marines and the CP agencies under
their command.

00:09:22.819 --> 00:09:26.629
However how do they keep authority over those
groups?

00:09:26.629 --> 00:09:30.059
After all there is no higher power backing
them up.

00:09:30.059 --> 00:09:32.660
Of course there is Imu, but people don't know
about her.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:38.270
If they truly were just Spandams, surely in
the 800 year history of the government, some

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.949
Marine or government agent would have tried
to usurp them.

00:09:41.949 --> 00:09:47.339
Or even the revolutionary army might have
gone straight for their heads.

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:53.139
Akainu surely wouldn't have listened to them,
if they didn't have anything to back up their

00:09:53.139 --> 00:09:54.139
authority.

00:09:54.139 --> 00:09:58.589
And yet Sengoku and Akainu never think about
actually going against them.

00:09:58.589 --> 00:10:00.179
At least so far.

00:10:00.179 --> 00:10:10.430
But I want you to notice just how calm the
Gorosei are at Sakazuki's insolence.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:18.069
Normally, people would be trembling like Coby
at an angry Sakazuki, but the Gorosei simply

00:10:18.069 --> 00:10:23.170
shrugg it off, mocking him and treating him
like a tempered child.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:29.720
Weaklings don't show this confidence, especially
since these five aren't stupid.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:35.459
And then they are casually meeting with one
of the most powerful pirates in the entire

00:10:35.459 --> 00:10:43.290
world, dismissing their guards.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:48.850
No matter what powers they have at their disposal,
the fact that they appear to have battle experience

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:54.610
and unwavering authority over people like
Akainu and Lucci proves to me, that they all

00:10:54.610 --> 00:11:00.410
must be immensely physically powerful, especially
after they realized that they could subscribe

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.139
to my channel for more weekly One Piece content.

00:11:03.139 --> 00:11:09.259
The big question I have always asked myself
is 'how evil are these guys'?

00:11:09.259 --> 00:11:10.749
Or are they evil at all?

00:11:10.749 --> 00:11:15.209
This is a truly interesting question, because
I think that other than doflamingo for example,

00:11:15.209 --> 00:11:18.939
the Gorosei are in a much more morally grey
area.

00:11:18.939 --> 00:11:24.379
On the one hand they lead a regime that uses
slavery, neglects and manipulates its people

00:11:24.379 --> 00:11:28.160
and orders the destruction of an entire island.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:38.519
But then Oda-sensei still throws in nuances
that make them appear more human.

00:11:38.519 --> 00:11:43.920
During the Ohara incident, at least some of
them seem pained with their decision.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.680
They actually wanted Jinbe to create a better
relationship with the fishmen and allowed

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.399
them access to the Reverie.

00:11:50.399 --> 00:11:56.240
And they clearly were not happy with Doflamingo's
actions, but couldn't do anything about it,

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:02.300
since he was a celestial dragon himself with
knowledge about the national treasure of Marijoe

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:05.119
that he could use as leverage against them.

00:12:05.119 --> 00:12:10.190
And they seem to work with Shanks to keep
the world balanced.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:16.000
This gets even more confusing when looking
at Oda-sensei's inspiration for all five of

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.000
them.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:21.360
What keeps fascinating me every time it think
about it, is that all five of them seem to

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.949
be inspired by influential historical political
figures.

00:12:25.949 --> 00:12:29.639
Most prominently we have one who looks like
Mahatma Gandhi.

00:12:29.639 --> 00:12:35.459
One of them looks like a young Abraham Lincoln,
one like Karl Marx, one like Michael Gorbachov

00:12:35.459 --> 00:12:40.889
and the one with the long beard like the Japanese
position Itagaki Taisuke.

00:12:40.889 --> 00:12:46.339
Now all of these figures represent very different
political ideologies and all of them had their

00:12:46.339 --> 00:12:52.709
flaws, but what unites all of them at least
from a historical perspective was that they

00:12:52.709 --> 00:13:01.540
are associated with giving people more freedom.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:06.980
Lincoln is known for ending slavery in the
US, Gandhi ended British Colonial Rule in

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:12.259
India, Marx' fundamental idea, that was later
strongly misused by multiple regimes, was

00:13:12.259 --> 00:13:17.610
the theory of liberty, stating that the freedom
of the people is the most important right,

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:21.869
that should not be exploited and controlled
by those with power and money.

00:13:21.869 --> 00:13:26.480
Gorbachov was the last president of the Soviet
Union, who with his ideas of glasnost and

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.750
perestroika (openness and restructuring) promoted
democratic thinking and liberty in Eastern

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.189
Europe that ultimately led to the collapse
of the Soviet Union.

00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:40.439
And finally Itagaki was leader of the Freedom
and People's Rights Movement and involved

00:13:40.439 --> 00:13:45.290
with the founding of the first democratic
political party in Japan.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:50.829
So either Oda-sensei is being very ironic
by basing the authoritarian rulers of the

00:13:50.829 --> 00:13:53.609
world on people fighting for freedom.

00:13:53.609 --> 00:13:56.970
Or there is something more to this.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:02.100
To me the main goal of the government seems
to be to keep the balance of the world.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:07.410
They meet with Shanks, buy weapons from Kaido
and dealt with mother caramel for powerful

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:09.139
orphans.

00:14:09.139 --> 00:14:20.149
Clearly they have no interest in getting rid
of the Yonko system, but rather promote it.

00:14:20.149 --> 00:14:24.760
There seem to be only two instances where
the government seems to feel threatened.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:29.619
One was the incident of Ohara, that might
have revealed the true history to the world,

00:14:29.619 --> 00:14:40.389
and the other was Imu's frustration with Luffy,
Vivi, Poseidon and Blackbeard.

00:14:40.389 --> 00:14:43.779
No kaido, no Big Mom, no Dragon.

00:14:43.779 --> 00:14:48.899
However all those 4 seem to have connections
to the void century, except Blackbeard, who

00:14:48.899 --> 00:14:54.079
seems to have connections to Rocks, who also
was a major threat to the government.

00:14:54.079 --> 00:14:58.970
Luffy's straw hat connects him to the giant
straw hat on Marijoe, Shirahishi is a ancient

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:05.439
weapon and Vivi is connected to Pluton and
the only of the 20 kingdoms, that didn't join

00:15:05.439 --> 00:15:07.249
the celestial dragons on the red line.

00:15:07.249 --> 00:15:12.119
As for shanks, I don't think he's plotting
with the government, but trying his best to

00:15:12.119 --> 00:15:17.899
ease the way for Luffy and keep the world
from falling apart before he has found the

00:15:17.899 --> 00:15:18.899
one piece.

00:15:18.899 --> 00:15:25.179
So are the Gorosei just interested in keeping
things as they are to keep living in comfort

00:15:25.179 --> 00:15:26.179
forever?

00:15:26.179 --> 00:15:29.129
They do seem to have a fairly stressful job
though.

00:15:29.129 --> 00:15:34.040
I really can't wait to find out what their
connection with Imu is.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:40.080
I think it would be a very interesting twist
if one of them, either Imu or the Gorosei

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:46.889
was actually a 'good guy' after all, keeping
the other in check.

00:15:46.889 --> 00:15:49.019
But let's talk about the immortality thing.

00:15:49.019 --> 00:15:53.989
There are actually a number of theories out
there that connect imu and the gorosei to

00:15:53.989 --> 00:15:55.049
immortality.

00:15:55.049 --> 00:16:00.199
One option being of course the OP OP no mi
that might have been used multiple times.

00:16:00.199 --> 00:16:03.899
Another theory is connected to the theme of
flowers.

00:16:03.899 --> 00:16:08.149
A golden flower that connected Imu and Nika
and the Lunarians.

00:16:08.149 --> 00:16:12.919
I should probably make a separate video just
about that idea.

00:16:12.919 --> 00:16:17.459
And the biggest theory with the most evidence
behind it is this video right here, where

00:16:17.459 --> 00:16:21.779
I explain all the reasons why imu and the
celestial dragons are immortal and what the

00:16:21.779 --> 00:16:24.499
secret behind that might be.

00:16:24.499 --> 00:16:29.119
You know, if you're interested.

